			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841862">
									

<p>This isn't a joke SCP. This is mainlister material, provided you write it well.</p>
<p>The most dangerous things the Foundation faces are never the doomsday cults or horrifying monsters- it's the ones involving phrases like &quot;Amateur Thaumaturge&quot; and &quot;unattended 9-year-old&quot;.</p>
<p>All you have to do is take everything you're thinking of, and pit it against an elite team of agents questioning the life decisions that have them under siege by badly drawn ninja dinosaurs and squirrels driving monster trucks.</p>
<p>Only thing really holding me back from an immediate greenlight is that I'd like to see a little more fleshing out of the plot. Don't need extreme detail or a full blown outline; just sell me on the idea that you have some sort of coherent plotline figured out between the notebook coming to life and the showdown with the Pikazilla OC. (For instance, where are the townsfolk in all of this, not to mention the kid and his dad?)</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Bonus points if you manage to have this end in some heartwarming moment without jumping the shark.</span></p>

							</div>

								
					
