<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard layout + Addenda</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
SCP-XXXX is a life-size wax replica of George Washington. Physically all looks normal excluding it's face, which has been disfigured, leaving only a pair of the president's famous wooden teeth visible. Object will actively roam and attempt to locate wood of any form. If the object senses wood within about a 10 meter radius (through unknown means), object will enter a frenzied state and produce a knife from within it's wax body, designated as SCP-XXXX-1. In the state, entity will attempt to dismantle any wooden matter in the area and begin whittling it down into &quot;wooden nickels&quot;. SCP-XXXX-1 is unnaturally efficient at carving wood, with object able to manufacture a coin about every 8 seconds. These coins, designated as SCP-XXXX-2, will upon physical human contact transfigure into a real coin. The coins will maintain this form for 78 hours after initial contact. The type of coin seems to be linked to the type of wood used (research ongoing). Researchers have also observed that entity will also instinctively pick at leaves, which upon human contact will briefly transfigure into the shape of paper currency before melting into pulp.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
A central focus is the implication that this anomalous object was likely artificially created through unknown means for the express purpose of producing counterfeit currency. Researchers speculate though that object is likely an unsuccessful prototype, evident by a number of &quot;flaws&quot; that would make a counterfeit operation difficult to achieve at scale. This leaves it open for the possibility of other similar objects having been made. Article will also detail the acquisition of the object and the discovery of a violent reaction the object has when it becomes conscious that it possesses wood on it's body (the disfigurement of it's face was a result of attempts to remove them).</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
I plan to attach a photo of the entity that will hopefully hook the reader into learning more and will draw them in further with the idea that this object was made for a criminal purpose by and unknown creator.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> N/A</p>

